      "cat-harness:section": "Task_TRA_SeedFuzzy",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-14: candidates are never a barrier to having a translation; a writer that adds candidates for an empty msgstr also writes the first candidate as its msgstr, marked fuzzy (stated in cat-harness-tools scripts/lib/translation-adjudication.ts, CANDIDATES_SCHEMA).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "Owner rulings, 2026-11-18, on per-block translation feedback: (1) a 🌐 pane on every page, source-language pages included, listing every locale's current translation, its status, chosen.how and chosen.by, the page's own locale first and the others collapsed; (2) proposals live in the translation-candidates/v1 sidecar, and any GitHub author's proposal is appended as a human candidate; (3) only an owner, member or collaborator adjudicates, everyone else proposes; (4) the auto-pick ranks official 0, adjudicated 1, human 2, translation platform 3, agent 4, machine translation 5, a QA failure adds 10, a stale candidate is never auto-picked, ties go to the newest; (5) an auto-pick is official only on an exact sourceText match. Hence Task_TRA_BlockPane, Task_TRA_Propose, Task_TRA_AutoPick and End_TRA_Adjudicated. The implementation is cat-harness-tools#2432.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-18",
        "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/pull/2432"
      ]
    }
